      "writtenOn": "2026-07-08T12:47:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we remove the per-call symbol lookup wrappers and let each consumer resolve and cache its IPFIX dependencies during initialization? Flowprobe, NAT, and IOAM currently need only the IPFIX main pointer and report add/delete function. In particular, NAT reaches `vlib_get_plugin_symbol()` for every exported event, causing repeated plugin hash lookups and `dlsym()` calls in the datapath. Resolving those two `ipfix_*` symbols once per consumer follows the existing DNS pattern and preserves the optional dependency. The other wrappers have no external in-tree users; if the consumer API grows later, they could be consolidated behind an `ipfix_get_api()` table.",
      "revId": "bbc8ec90ef34db45d34264d935cf5602fc91d3e5",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
